<pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.05" change_id="I56587a151b4c7bb0a2e71698799d4ef9dd2c436a" commit="a66b25d3ce024bf1421cb24210e4a4efe48eaa9e" commit_message="UPSTREAM: Add newlines at the end of all coreboot files  BUG=None BRANCH=None TEST=None  Change-Id: I56587a151b4c7bb0a2e71698799d4ef9dd2c436a Signed-off-by: Martin Roth &lt;martinroth@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://review.coreboot.org/15974 Tested-by: build bot (Jenkins) Reviewed-by: Kysti Mlkki &lt;kyosti.malkki@gmail.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/366301 Commit-Ready: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="366301" owner_email="furquan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/01/366301/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.05" change_id="Ic5073304d3c8e6452ec072ecece036beac26323a" commit="b2e61253d53c9be46ded905111f8f2b9711a7965" commit_message="UPSTREAM: Remove non-ascii &amp; unprintable characters  These non-ascii &amp; unprintable characters aren't needed.  BUG=None BRANCH=None TEST=None  Change-Id: Ic5073304d3c8e6452ec072ecece036beac26323a Signed-off-by: Martin Roth &lt;martinroth@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://review.coreboot.org/15977 Tested-by: build bot (Jenkins) Reviewed-by: Omar Pakker Reviewed-by: Paul Menzel &lt;paulepanter@users.sourceforge.net&gt; Reviewed-by: Stefan Reinauer &lt;stefan.reinauer@coreboot.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/366302 Commit-Ready: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="366302" owner_email="furquan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/02/366302/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.05" change_id="I314353fae8ea30573257e0a7007b5cb4ce39d4b8" commit="440c3634aa853c7a8e4dd21f02a9a275f0b4b62a" commit_message="UPSTREAM: soc/intel/common: Fix build error in reset.c  Fix build error caused by macro substitution in the function definition when the Kconfig value HAVE_HARD_RESET is not selected.  src/soc/intel/common/reset.c:36:21: error: macro &quot;hard_reset&quot; passed 1 arguments, but takes just 0  void hard_reset(void)                      ^ src/soc/intel/common/reset.c:37:1: error: expected '=', ',', ';', 'asm' or '__attribute__' before '{' token  {  ^ make: *** [build/bootblock/soc/intel/common/reset.o] Error 1  TEST=Build and run on Galileo Gen2  BUG=None BRANCH=None  Change-Id: I314353fae8ea30573257e0a7007b5cb4ce39d4b8 Signed-off-by: Lee Leahy &lt;leroy.p.leahy@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://review.coreboot.org/15988 Tested-by: build bot (Jenkins) Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/366303 Commit-Ready: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="366303" owner_email="furquan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/03/366303/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I18897cfc04726e6aeda59f4c6e742d7a0037cf80" commit="8befb4b24b2b2eaabeca6096975465375d2dc5a4" commit_message="Add new &quot;hang&quot; option to crash command  The crash command is used to intentionally invoke various failure modes in a running system. This adds one more (and cleans up the command slightly). The &quot;crash hang&quot; command does the same thing as &quot;crash watchdog&quot;, except that it disables interrupts first. Some SoCs may require special handling to recover from that case.  BUG=none BRANCH=none TEST=make buildall; run on Cr50 hardware  Invoked all the options to the crash command, observed that the appropriate response occurred in each case (a stack trace if possible, followed by a reboot).  Change-Id: I18897cfc04726e6aeda59f4c6e742d7a0037cf80 Signed-off-by: Bill Richardson &lt;wfrichar@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/366127 Reviewed-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@google.com&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="366127" owner_email="wfrichar@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/27/366127/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I46daed29d7e37bda9034a3486127bed0ea25f803" commit="0396793366e832e62348e857e55f1c13ac234b6f" commit_message="g: Decode more reasons for chip reset  There are few reasons why the SoC may reboot which we haven't been reporting (they just show up as &quot;[Reset cause: other]&quot;). This adds a bit of decoding to explain some of those &quot;other&quot; reasons.  BUG=none BRANCH=none TEST=make buildall; try on Cr50  I tested one of the new reasons using &quot;crash hang&quot;. It shows up correctly as &quot;{Reset cause: security]&quot;. I haven't specifically tested all of the new reasons, but since this is basically just a change to console message they should work too. I'll double-check those cases once some blocking bugs are fixed.  Change-Id: I46daed29d7e37bda9034a3486127bed0ea25f803 Signed-off-by: Bill Richardson &lt;wfrichar@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/366400 Reviewed-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="366400" owner_email="wfrichar@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/00/366400/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I268abe40e744c9dace0ded9082abbf1a52913f4c" commit="a0ae0350071f84075d1c23d645219f2ee10f607c" commit_message="Support EV_MSC event types for ChromeOS  A vendor reported the remote chromeos support crashing when EV_MSC events were emitted by their touch device.  This seems to be due to evtest reporting those events as hexidecimal values instead of base-10. According to evtest's source there are only 2 events that it does this for, so this CL adds in a check for those events in an attempt to parse them correctly.  BUG=chromium:627506 TEST=manually tested, then verified by the vendor  Change-Id: I268abe40e744c9dace0ded9082abbf1a52913f4c Signed-off-by: Charlie Mooney &lt;charliemooney@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/359945 Reviewed-by: Andrew de los Reyes &lt;adlr@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="359945" owner_email="charliemooney@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/touch_firmware_test" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/touch_firmware_test" ref="refs/changes/45/359945/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I98c223dff61b0d851e6c6fa6a94e04a68c5d3044" commit="4e40508e05fe160c68f83f30442b64698b215c3e" commit_message="Revise tag in platform_ExternalUsbperipherals usb_detect control file  BUG=chromium:621966 TEST=None  Change-Id: I98c223dff61b0d851e6c6fa6a94e04a68c5d3044 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/361641 Commit-Ready: Helen Zhang &lt;helenzhang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Helen Zhang &lt;helenzhang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kalin Stoyanov &lt;kalin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="361641" owner_email="helenzhang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/41/361641/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ie7c09ae6e783ddb85bb1e5ecc2d2d05489231449" commit="84b2773acf17b255cad99b6cd8ade35d6fde3616" commit_message="UPSTREAM: mac80211: Remove MPP table entries with MPath  Make the mesh_path_del() function remove all mpp table entries that are proxied by the removed mesh path.  Acked-by: Bob Copeland &lt;me@bobcopeland.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Henning Rogge &lt;henning.rogge@fkie.fraunhofer.de&gt; Signed-off-by: Johannes Berg &lt;johannes.berg@intel.com&gt;  (cherry-picked from mac80211 bf5a70e105820eb214d3f33376cf6a3011d2e20c)  BUG=b:29897970 TEST=manually on whrilwinds and gale  Change-Id: Ie7c09ae6e783ddb85bb1e5ecc2d2d05489231449 Signed-off-by: Julan Hsu &lt;julanhsu@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/365483 Reviewed-by: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="365483" owner_email="julanhsu@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/83/365483/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I0b3b41861f15fc335469f30c195e02d0301f71b8" commit="beaafc2cdfedf22d8114815e2a1a5f82f95b4865" commit_message="UPSTREAM: mac80211: let unused MPP table entries timeout  Remember the last time when a mpp table entry is used for rx or tx and remove them after MESH_PATH_EXPIRE time.  Acked-by: Bob Copeland &lt;me@bobcopeland.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Henning Rogge &lt;henning.rogge@fkie.fraunhofer.de&gt; Signed-off-by: Johannes Berg &lt;johannes.berg@intel.com&gt;  (cherry-picked from mac80211 ab1c7906b0bead549065a3a2def5aeda21818c99)  BUG=b:29354388 TEST=manually on whirlwinds and gales  Change-Id: I0b3b41861f15fc335469f30c195e02d0301f71b8 Signed-off-by: Julan Hsu &lt;julanhsu@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/365482 Reviewed-by: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="365482" owner_email="julanhsu@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/82/365482/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I74c375f260e6999707f70838cf8524e1122d2a22" commit="a21e22956d2dd99c5abeae9b8abd70dc64f90d73" commit_message="UPSTREAM: mac80211: mesh: handle failed alloc for rmc cache  In the unlikely case that mesh_rmc_init() fails with -ENOMEM, the rmc pointer will be left as NULL but the interface is still operational because ieee80211_mesh_init_sdata() is not allowed to fail.  If this happens, we would blindly dereference rmc when checking whether a multicast frame is in the cache.  Instead just drop the frames in the forwarding path.  Signed-off-by: Bob Copeland &lt;me@bobcopeland.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Johannes Berg &lt;johannes.berg@intel.com&gt;  (cherry-picked from mac80211 0aa7fabbd5d9da1f8a8fdc3e2837c532bcfa5664)  BUG=b:29897970 TEST=manually on whirlwinds  Change-Id: I74c375f260e6999707f70838cf8524e1122d2a22 Signed-off-by: Julan Hsu &lt;julanhsu@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/365481 Reviewed-by: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="365481" owner_email="julanhsu@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/81/365481/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I09a1f82dcdad6e3130f92b623947243de52c72b7" commit="123c9cfac09482cb2a215fb4bfeb78be06e4c660" commit_message="Gale: Add initial FAFT config  BUG=none BRANCH=none TEST=&quot;test_that --board=gale DUT_IP_ADDR f:.*firmware_InvalidUSB/control&quot;  Change-Id: I09a1f82dcdad6e3130f92b623947243de52c72b7 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/366125 Commit-Ready: Julio Diez &lt;jdiez@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Julio Diez &lt;jdiez@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Suresh Rajashekara &lt;sureshraj@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="366125" owner_email="jdiez@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/25/366125/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Icbd1ed3d79e9d84fe490ca3037e0ebf7a4cbd4d2" commit="335ed971537bb1b59f9d54a33fcdace1a61740be" commit_message="autotest: Disable kernel_TPMPing until it works more reliably  This test wasn't running on 3.10, 3.14, or 3.18 anyway due to an incorrect version check.  Then it was failing on 4.4, but because of missing log spam and not because of a missing feature.  We could fix the version check and add the log spam to 4.4 but it sounds like folks would like a better way to check this than extra kernel log spam anyway.  For now we'll disable.  BUG=chromium:634341 TEST=emerge-${BOARD} -pv autotest-tests-tpm  Change-Id: Icbd1ed3d79e9d84fe490ca3037e0ebf7a4cbd4d2 Signed-off-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/366135 Reviewed-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Luigi Semenzato &lt;semenzato@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="366135" owner_email="dianders@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/35/366135/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><lkgm version="8676.0.0-rc3"/></manifest>